For this benches directly, we can use it to compare normal 
implementation for benches provided in use test::Bencher against
the one we have for criterion. 
This will allows us to compare the two.

However, criterion privides many other tools that not only 
gives us speedy bench tests, but also plot charts and information
against other types. This is a great tool and we can explore this
more later.

Look at the documentation to know more.

If we want to see the html representation of our criterion function
output, the report dir, located inside target/criterion should have
the entry page to all the generated output.
